slime patch for Megatron-LM @ 9e68a11bd

Port of docker/patch/latest/megatron.patch (written against Megatron-LM
1dcf0dafa884ad52ffb243625717a3471643e087, mcore 0.16.0rc0) onto
9e68a11bd "Merge upstream main for follow-up validation".

Apply with:

    cd <Megatron-LM checkout at 9e68a11bd>
    git apply --3way /path/to/megatron_9e68a11bd.patch

WHAT CHANGED RELATIVE TO THE REFERENCE PATCH
--------------------------------------------

Dropped -- upstream now does the same thing natively:

  * gpt_model.py / multi_token_prediction.py MTP rework. Upstream moved the
    MTP loss into process_mtp_loss(), which already derives labels from
    input_ids by rolling left when labels is None ("e.g. RL training"), rolls
    loss_mask in lockstep, and detaches the heads under
    config.mtp_detach_heads. Only the parts slime still needs are kept: the
    mtp_kwargs plumbing, routing mtp_labels in as input_ids, forcing the
    detach on that path, and skipping MTP entirely when nothing was handed in.
  * multi_token_prediction._checkpointed_forward tensor-flattening wrapper.
    Upstream rewrote it with a custom_forward closure that already passes only
    tensors positionally.
  * decoder_input.detach() / make_viewless_tensor(keep_graph=False) in the MTP
    layer. Upstream gates the same behaviour on config.mtp_detach_heads.
  * parallel_state.py "import torch.distributed as dist". Unused there, and no
    slime code reads parallel_state.dist.

Relocated:

  * trust_remote_code=True moved from megatron/training/tokenizer/tokenizer.py
    (deleted upstream) to
    megatron/core/tokenizers/text/libraries/huggingface_tokenizer.py.
  * post_self_attn_layernorm / post_mlp_layernorm are wired through
    get_gpt_layer_with_transformer_engine_submodules() and use
    backend.layer_norm() instead of a direct TENorm import (TENorm is no longer
    imported in gpt_layer_specs.py; for the TE backend backend.layer_norm()
    *is* TENorm).
  * The DDP cpu-backup flags go through training.wrap_model_chunks_with_ddp(),
    which replaced the inline DP(...) list comprehension in get_model().
  * The MCoreLoadPlanner allow_partial_load=True is added alongside the
    flatten_state_dict/flatten_sharded_tensors kwargs the call site grew.
  * The fused MLA yarn-RoPE kernels were renamed
    _mla_rope_{fwd,bwd}_kv_split_kernel and grew a REMOVE_INTERLEAVING branch;
    the head-masking / k_dim_ceil / v_dim==0 fixes are applied to both branches.

Added -- the reference patch is missing these and would AttributeError:

  * --post-self-attn-layernorm and --post-mlp-layernorm. The reference patch
    sets kw_args['post_self_attn_layernorm'] = args.post_self_attn_layernorm
    but no longer declares the flags (docker/patch/v0.5.9 still did). Here they
    are declared implicitly: arguments are now generated from TransformerConfig
    fields (ArgumentGroupFactory, mcore PR #2896), so adding the two fields to
    TransformerConfig also creates the two CLI flags, and
    core_transformer_config_from_args copies them back automatically. The
    explicit kw_args[...] lines are therefore not needed.
  * --use-gated-attention is deliberately NOT re-added, following the same
    reasoning that reverted it from the checkout in 325333212: it is not a
    TransformerConfig field, nothing in Megatron or slime ever reads it, and
    slime parses with ignore_unknown_args=True, so the bundle's flag is dropped
    without an error. Job 18743074 confirms it on this commit -- the run parsed
    fine with no such flag declared, and the real gate came through as
    attention_output_gate=True from --attention-output-gate. megatron/training/
    arguments.py is therefore untouched by this patch.

  * The two GLM-4 layernorm hunks in transformer_layer.py are guarded on the
    layernorm not being IdentityOp. The reference patch unpacks
    `attention_output_with_bias` and `mlp_output_with_bias` unconditionally,
    which assumes every TransformerLayer has both a real attention and a real
    MLP. A hybrid stack breaks that on both sides: its MLP/MoE layers are
    TransformerLayers with no self_attention (megatron/core/ssm/mlp_layer.py,
    `class MLPLayer(TransformerLayer)`), and its attention layers carry no mlp,
    so in each case the value is a bare [s, b, h] tensor and unpacking it into
    two names iterates the sequence dimension -- `ValueError: too many values to
    unpack (expected 2)`. Job 18809189 died on the first MoE layer of
    Nemotron-3's 88-layer pattern, 23.8 s into its first forward, with the
    checkpoint already loaded and resharded. Upstream never unpacks there; it
    passes the value to the bda step, which is IdentityFuncOp on those layers.
    Nothing in this tree sets either layernorm -- only GLM-4 does -- so the
    guard makes both hunks no-ops everywhere they are not wanted. The same bug
    is in the reference patch for 0.16 and is worth fixing there too.

  * megatron/training/training.py no longer sets torch_memory_saver.hook_mode.
    0.20 grew a second copy of the line the reference patch disables in
    inference/contexts/dynamic_context.py, this time in a module every slime
    actor imports (slime/backends/megatron_utils/model.py imports get_model from
    it). hook_mode is process-global and is consumed the first time TMS
    initializes, so the import silently overrode the preload hook slime installs
    for --offload-train (LD_PRELOAD + TMS_INIT_ENABLE=1, slime/ray/
    actor_group.py). The process then holds two TMS backends -- the preloaded
    library interposing cudaMalloc and a torch-mode library behind the Python
    object -- torch_memory_saver.disable() clears the region flag on the wrong
    one, and tensors allocated in that window stay VMM-backed, so the colocated
    weight sync dies exporting a CUDA IPC handle (storage._share_cuda_ ->
    cudaErrorInvalidValue). Jobs 18797342 and 18797223 died there at rollout 0,
    1.8 s and 2.2 s into their first update_weights. HAVE_TORCH_MEMORY_SAVER is
    set False alongside it, as in the dynamic_context hunk: in training.py it
    gates only Megatron's own --rl-offload-inference-model-weights-when-idle
    path, and slime's rollout engine is SGLang.

Behaviour notes:

  * _postprocess now skips MTP when neither labels nor mtp_kwargs['mtp_labels']
    is given. Stock Megatron pretraining/SFT (labels given) is unaffected; what
    is disabled is upstream's derive-labels-from-input_ids path for callers
    that pass labels=None and no mtp_kwargs, which is what slime wants when
    mtp_num_layers > 0 but enable_mtp_training is off (MTP weights kept only
    for SGLang EAGLE speculative decoding).
  * _batched_p2p_ops drops the process group. prev/next_pipeline_rank are
    already global ranks, so peers are unchanged; only the communicator is.

